          "id": "36e1d7c292ad268c3baa2e75f6f3b2cbb138aea0",
          "message": "chore: upgrade to lindera 5.0.1 (#5887)\n\n# Ticket(s) Closed\n\n- Closes #\n\nSupersedes #5877, rebased onto current `main` and moved from 5.0.0 to\n5.0.1.\nSubstantially mitigates #4840, and likely removes the need for #5125 —\nsee below.\n\n## What\n\n- `lindera` 1.5.1 → 5.0.1, plus the new `lindera-analysis` 5.0.1 crate\nthat the filter chain moved into.\n- Feature renames: `embedded-*` → `embed-*`. The `compress` feature no\nlonger exists in 5.x.\n- Imports in `tokenizers/src/lindera.rs` split between `lindera`\n(segmenter, dictionaries) and `lindera-analysis` (character filters,\ntoken filters, `Tokenizer`).\n- `nix/pg_search.nix`: `LINDERA_CACHE` →\n`LINDERA_BUILD_DICTIONARY_CACHE_DIR`.\n- `tests`: tokio `time` and `sync` declared explicitly.\n- **No CI changes.** The diff does not touch `.github/` at all — the\n`test-pg_search` runner volume stays at 80GB, exactly as on `main`.\n\n## Why\n\nThe upgrade drops 56 crates from the Lindera compilation, one of the\nslowest parts of our builds — the `reqwest`/`rustls`/`quinn` download\nstack the 1.x dictionary crates pulled in at build time, along with\n`tower`, `security-framework`, `schannel`, and `yada`.\n\n#5877 stalled at 5.0.0 because the build tree bloated: lindera 4 and\n5.0.0 bind the embedded dictionary bytes to a `const`, and a `const`\nbody is encoded into the crate's metadata at roughly 4x the payload.\nBuilding the workspace debug and release both filled the 80GB volume.\n\n5.0.1 binds them to a `static` instead. That is the *entire* source diff\nbetween the two releases — `lindera`, `lindera-analysis`, and the three\ndictionary crates are byte-identical between 5.0.0 and 5.0.1.\n\n### Build footprint\n\nThree builds on one runner, `cargo build -p tokenizers`, resolved\n`lindera-dictionary` asserted per configuration:\n\n| config | lindera-dictionary | release rlib | release rmeta | linked\ntest bin | target/ total | vs main |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| `main` | `1.5.1` | 53 MB | 4 MB | 56 MB | 3084 MB | — |\n| `5.0.0` | `5.0.0` | 1036 MB | 831 MB | 210 MB | 6776 MB | 2.20x |\n| `5.0.1` | `5.0.1` | 401 MB | 196 MB | 210 MB | 4235 MB | 1.37x |\n\n5.0.1 gives back **2541 MB** per build tree. The rmeta column shows the\nmechanism: 831 MB → 196 MB, the `const` body no longer being copied into\ncrate metadata.\n\n### Runtime: this also mitigates #4840\n\nThe removal of `compress` is not a regression — it is a fix. On 1.5.1\nthe compressed path expands to `static Lazy<Vec<u8>>`, so **every\nprocess inflates the whole dictionary into private heap**, which is\nexactly the per-worker cold start #4840 reports. On 5.0.1 the bytes are\n`static &[u8]` in `.rodata`, passed as `Data::Static` and read zero-copy\nvia the new `DaTrust::Trusted` path (`deserialize_unchecked`, no\nvalidation pass) — demand-paged and shared across all backends.\n\nMeasured, both configurations on one runner, median of 3, one fresh\nprocess per reading:\n\n| tokenizer | `main` (1.5.1) cold | `5.0.1` cold | speedup | warm |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| `korean_lindera` (ko-dic) | 282.7 ms | 26.2 ms | **11x** | 0.04 ms |\n| `japanese_lindera` (ipadic) | 141.2 ms | 8.0 ms | **18x** | 0.01 ms |\n| `chinese_lindera` (cc-cedict) | 94.8 ms | 4.3 ms | **22x** | 0.01 ms |\n\nThis is fix direction 3 from #4840 (\"switch to a pure-mmap\nrepresentation\"), reached without the install/packaging work in #5125 —\nand in the shape preferred in [that\ndiscussion](https://github.com/paradedb/paradedb/pull/5125#issuecomment-4930339903):\nbundled in the binary, nothing installed alongside.\n\n**It does not take the cost to zero.** ko-dic still spends ~26 ms, so\nparallel queries against Korean indexes keep a real if much smaller\nfixed cost. #4840 should be re-measured end to end rather than assumed\nfixed, and jieba is untouched — always a separate item in #5125's scope.\n\n### Binary size\n\n`pg_search.so` grows: 5.x has no `compress`, so the dictionaries embed\nuncompressed. #5125\n[measured](https://github.com/paradedb/paradedb/pull/5125#issuecomment-4928427787)\nthe equivalent change at +146 MiB release. Note that #5125 ships 148 MiB\nof dictionary files alongside the extension anyway, so total\ndistribution size is roughly a wash; embedding moves those bytes into\nthe `.so` rather than adding them.\n\n## How\n\nThe Nix change is load-bearing. `nix/pg_search.nix` copies the\ndictionary tarballs into a cache directory so `build.rs` does not reach\nthe network inside the sandbox. Lindera 5 renamed the variable that\npoints at it from `LINDERA_CACHE` to\n`LINDERA_BUILD_DICTIONARY_CACHE_DIR`; the old name is no longer read at\nall, so without the rename the sandboxed build tries to download and\nfails. Layout and tarball hashes are unchanged.\n\nThe tests crate gains explicit tokio `time` and `sync` features — used\nby `joinscan_concurrent.rs`, `mpp_cancel.rs`, and `parallel.rs`,\npreviously supplied by feature unification through the `reqwest` stack\nthat the 1.x dictionary crates pulled in.\n\n## Tests\n\nFull suite green, including:\n\n- `test-pg_search` — all six jobs (PG15–18, system and pgrx, arm64 and\namd64) **on the unchanged 80GB volume**. No job hit `insufficient disk\nspace`.\n- `test-pg_search-nix` — exercises the renamed cache variable inside the\nNix sandbox.\n- `test-pg_search-upgrade`, `test-dst-crate`, and all lints.\n\nThe reading-form tests in `tokenizers/src/lindera.rs` carry over from\n#5877 unchanged, including the assertion that no token indexes as the\n`*` placeholder.\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Philippe Noël <21990816+philippemnoel@users.noreply.github.com>",
