          "message": "feat: vector search (#5215)\n\n# Ticket(s) Closed\n\n- Closes #\n\n## What\n\nThe BM25 index now supports the pgvector `vector` type:\n\n```sql\nCREATE INDEX on embeddings USING bm25 (id, text_field, embeddings vector_cosine_ops) WITH (key_field=id);\n```\n\nNote that we follow the same `opclass` convention as `pgvector`.\n\nInternally, vectors are backed by a SPANN-style index. They sit\nalongside non-vector types (text, numeric, etc) so queries with filters,\ntext search ordered by vector similarity can be pushed down to one\nefficient scan of the BM25 index.\n\nOnce released, this PR makes `pgvector` a required extension, so\nupgrading will require `pgvector` to already have been installed.\n\n## Why\n\n## How\n\nBacked by internal spec doc.\n\n## Tests\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Ruchir Raj <ruchirraj24@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: paradedb-github-app[bot] <282009505+paradedb-github-app[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>",
          "timestamp": "2026-07-23T14:05:22-07:00",
