          "distinct": true,
          "id": "3524cbc398dc0ffe6dba13eb2aef5b91173b2aeb",
          "message": "fix: Declare partitions from our table provider (#5657)\n\n## What\n\nPreviously, we always exposed `UnknownPartitioning(1)` out of our\n`TableProvider`, which produced one partition.\n\nThis change moves to exposing `UnknownPartitioning(min(num_segments,\nnum_workers))`, and adds a `TaskEstimator` that will cause `df-d` to\nproduce a task per partition.\n\n## Why\n\n`datafusion-distributed` attempts to create tasks based on the number of\npartitions of the data that are available. We previously were declaring\nthat only 1 partition existed, and were then scaling that up to N worker\npartitions via:\n```\nBroadcastExec: input_partitions=1, consumer_tasks=3, output_partitions=3\n```\n\nThis change aligns us with converting `UnknownPartitioning` to `Range`\npartitioning in the near future, and results in plans that better\ndescribe what we'd like to be happening.\n\n## Tests\n\nBenchmarks improve slightly for 100k and 1mm rows, and are unchanged for\n20mm rows.",
          "timestamp": "2026-07-23T14:54:11-07:00",
