          "distinct": true,
          "id": "c9395676e2299d2b156ae827161efdd15f08486a",
          "message": "chore: use `paradedb` as the index access method name everywhere (#5916)\n\nTicket(s) Closed: N/A\n\n## What\n\n`paradedb` is the primary name for the access method; `bm25` is a\nbackwards-compatible alias. This swaps every `USING bm25` in the repo\nover to `USING paradedb`:\n\n- `stressgres/suites/*.toml` (all six suites) and\n`stressgres/src/sqlscanner.rs`\n- `pg_search/tests/pg_regress/` — `sql/` and `expected/` in lockstep\n- `tests/tests/`, `tests/src/fixtures/`\n- `pg_search/src/` — `#[pg_test]` SPI setup, doc comments, and the two\nuser-facing messages in `api/operator.rs`\n- `docs/legacy/**` code blocks, `benchmarks/datasets/*/indexes/*.sql`,\n`.github/scripts/create_code_snippet_indexes.sql`\n\n`expected/vector_unsupported_types.out` also picks up the AM name in the\nerror text: `operator class \"halfvec_l2_ops\" does not exist for access\nmethod \"paradedb\"`.\n\nDeliberately left on `bm25`, where the name is the point rather than\nincidental:\n\n- the `CREATE ACCESS METHOD` and opclass DDL in `postgres/mod.rs`,\n`api/operator.rs` and `sql/pg_search--0.24.3--0.25.0.sql` that define\nthe alias — both AMs need their own opclasses\n- `pg_regress/{sql,expected}/paradedb_am`, which asserts the two names\nshare a handler and collide on the single-index guard\n- `docs/changelog/{0.21.5,0.21.6,0.25.0}.mdx`, plus\n`.github/scripts/verify/`, which extracts runnable snippets from them\n- the sentence in `docs/documentation/indexing/create-index.mdx`\ndocumenting the alias\n- `.github/actions/test-pg_search-upgrade/*/setup.sql`, which runs\nagainst a checked-out prior tag that has no `paradedb` AM\n\n## Why\n\nConsistency — the docs already lead with `USING paradedb`, so the test\nsuites and fixtures should too.\n\n## How\n\nMechanical rewrite. `cargo fmt --all` re-wrapped eight lines that\ncrossed 100 cols after the rename.\n\n## Tests\n\nNot run locally — the pg_regress `expected/` files were updated by the\nsame rewrite rather than regenerated from a run, so CI is the check\nhere.\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01JA8yXSnnezVMkZwvjBVKgX\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>",
