          "id": "a1dbb64a620cdc0c3dc10f7180fa03e85fc091f5",
          "message": "test: extract a `dst` crate for the Antithesis SDK integration (#5639)\n\npg_search and stressgres each carried their own `dst` module wrapping\n`antithesis_sdk`, with duplicated init and feature gating. Consolidate\nthat into one `dst` crate: a single place that depends on the SDK,\nbehind a single `enabled` feature flag.\n\nThe crate is off by default and compiles to nothing when `enabled` is\nunset. The assertion macros expand to a dead `if false { … }` that still\nname-resolves and type-checks their arguments (so the same source\ncompiles identically with or without the feature), `GhostState<T>` is a\nzero-sized type, `observe!` closures are type-checked but never run, and\n`init()` is a no-op — a consumer that does not opt in never links the\nSDK. With `enabled` on, everything forwards to `antithesis_sdk`.\n\nIt wraps exactly what main uses today — `init`, and the `reachable` /\n`unreachable` / `always` / `always_or_unreachable` / `sometimes` asserts\n(two generator macros stamp out the wrappers so each isn't hand-written\ntwice) — plus `observe!` and `GhostState<T>` ported from precept\n(orbitinghail/precept), so read-only property blocks and property-only\nghost state sit on top of the official SDK rather than precept.\n\nBecause the crate self-gates, consumers no longer need their own `dst`\nmodule or `#[cfg(feature = \"dst\")]` dance — they depend on `dst` and\ncall it directly:\n\n- pg_search depends on `dst` (its `dst` feature just flips\n`dst/enabled`). The background-merge crash report is now an inline\n`observe!` at the call site in merge.rs; `merge_crash_details` (which\ninspects pgrx `CaughtError`) lives beside it rather than in the generic\ncrate. No pg_search `dst` module.\n- stressgres depends on `dst` with `enabled` always on, matching its\ncurrent unconditional SDK linking; its two liveness assertions are\ninlined at their call sites. No stressgres `dst` module.\n\nNo behavior change; this is groundwork so the correctness-property and\ncoverage branches can rebase onto a single shared crate.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>",
