          "id": "82ed3b1858937742a23e2c23f8c6a0c5f4f21d45",
          "message": "chore: remove dead code and correct stale comments (#5815)\n\nDeletes code the compiler already knew was dead: the unreferenced\n`user_session_logs` test fixture,\n`CustomPathBuilder::clear_flags`/`add_custom_path` (and the\n`custom_paths` list they were the only writers of), and five unused\nhook-arg accessors. Dropping the fixture left `serde` unused in the\n`tests` crate, so that dependency goes too.\n\nCorrects comments that no longer matched the code: `utils.rs` claimed\nxmax is set to a `deleting_xid` that doesn't exist (it's\n`FrozenTransactionId`) and that delete files get `.mark_deleted()`\n(they're re-added as recyclable entries); the `storage/mod.rs`\nblock-layout header still described block 0 as the merge lock with fixed\nmetadata block numbers, when block 0 is the MetaPage and those numbers\nnow live in it; `translator.rs` claimed all casts return `None`, when\nvalue-preserving `RelabelType` and text-family `CoerceViaIO` are looked\nthrough. Plus three wrong identifiers: `PgSearchScanState` ->\n`Bm25ScanState`, `SEGMENT_METAS_START` -> `segment_metas()`,\n`MvccDirectory` -> `MVCCDirectory`.\n\nThe `ambulkdelete_epoch` fields on `Bm25ScanState` and\n`ParallelAggregationWorker` looked dead here but are read by enterprise,\nso they stay.\n\nNo behaviour change. `cargo check`, `clippy`, `fmt --check` and\n`machete` are clean on `pg_search` and the `tests` crate.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: paradedb-github-app[bot] <282009505+paradedb-github-app[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>",
