          "id": "f5b60b28835714484e30d344690e284560d397ce",
          "message": "fix(schemas): grant PUBLIC USAGE, not ALL, on paradedb and pdb schemas (#5897)\n\nThe `paradedb` and `pdb` schemas shipped with `GRANT ALL TO PUBLIC`,\nwhich includes `CREATE` — but PUBLIC only needs `USAGE` to reference our\noperators/types, every object in them is owner-created at install, and\nnothing in the charts creates there, so `CREATE` just lets any role\nsquat inside our own schemas. Grants `USAGE` instead and revokes\n`CREATE` in the `0.25.1 → 0.25.2` migration; stacked on #5896, retarget\nto `main` once it lands.\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Philippe Noël <21990816+philippemnoel@users.noreply.github.com>",
