          "id": "bd30a73f3e17f2e759210e4fbb2821b5c70d875a",
          "message": "fix: Run final build merge even when the last insert flushed at the doc cap (#5971)\n\nWhen a table's row count is an exact multiple of the per-segment doc cap\n(always 1000 for vector indexes), the last insert flushes the final\nsegment and leaves the writer with no pending segment. `writer.commit()`\nreturned `None`, and the final `try_merge(true)` — gated inside `if let\nSome(...)` — was silently skipped, leaving every flushed segment\nunmerged. A 1M-row vector build with `target_segment_count = 1` produced\n1000 segments of 1000 docs each.\n\nThe final merge now runs unconditionally at commit. Verified on the\ncohere 1m benchmark table: 1 segment of 1M docs after the fix. Added a\n`pg_test` covering the exact-multiple case.",
