          "id": "2224bd73fe9805593dc5b4aee753ea7b0a0e10a3",
          "message": "fix: use the scan's MVCC snapshot for query-visible mutable segments (#5365) (#5414)\n\n# Ticket(s) Closed\n\n- Part of #5365 (query-side; the VACUUM/ambulkdelete side is #5402)\n\n## What\n\nQuery-visible mutable segment materialization (`index_memory_segment`\nfor\n`MvccSatisfies::Snapshot` / `ParallelWorker`) now fetches each heap\ntuple with\nthe scan's **active MVCC snapshot** instead of `SnapshotAny`.\n\n## Why\n\nThe issue calls out two distinct code paths. This is the query side:\n\n> Query-visible mutable segment materialization must not fetch heap\ntuples with\n> `SnapshotAny`, because it can select `DEAD` / `RECENTLY_DEAD` versions\nwhose\n> external TOAST rows are not safely visible to the active TOAST\nsnapshot.\n\n`SnapshotAny` can hand back a `DEAD`/`RECENTLY_DEAD` tuple version whose\nexternal\nTOAST chunks have already been (or are concurrently being) reclaimed by\nVACUUM.\n`pg_detoast_datum` then fails:\n\n```\nERROR: missing chunk number 0 for toast value ... in pg_toast_...\nERROR: unexpected chunk number 196 (expected 0) for toast value ... in pg_toast_...\n```\n\nPinning the parent heap buffer does **not** protect against this — as\nthe issue\nnotes, TOAST lives in a separate relation and is read with\n`SnapshotToast`:\n\n> the parent heap tuple pin is not sufficient ... Normal queries protect\nTOAST\n> through an active/registered MVCC snapshot.\n\n## How\n\nIn `index_memory_segment`, thread the `MvccSatisfies` style down from\n`MVCCDirectory::file_entry` and classify the materialization:\n\n- **Query-visible (`Snapshot` / `ParallelWorker`)** — fetch each ctid\nwith\n`GetActiveSnapshot()`. A tuple visible to that registered snapshot has\nits\n  TOAST protected (the snapshot holds back the global xmin horizon), so\ndetoasting is safe. Tuples not visible to the snapshot are indexed as\nempty\ndocuments. Because a mutable segment is materialized lazily *inside* the\nscan,\nthis is exactly the snapshot the scan uses for ctid visibility, so a\nctid\nindexed empty here is also filtered out by the scan — query results are\nunchanged. The materialized `RamDirectory` is cached per-`MVCCDirectory`\n(per-scan), not shared across snapshots, so per-snapshot materialization\nis\n  correct.\n- **Maintenance (`Mergeable`, etc.)** — unchanged: keep `SnapshotAny` +\n`HeapTupleSatisfiesVacuum`, because the resulting segment must contain\nevery\n  live ctid (it serves future snapshots).\n\n## Tests\n\n- New `pg_regress` test `mutable-toast-query`: a mutable segment holding\nlive,\nupdated, and deleted large-toasted rows must return exactly the rows\nvisible to\n  the querying statement (and detoasting the visible rows must succeed).\n- Existing `mutable-toast` and all other mutable-segment regress tests\n(`segmented_topk`, `join_sort_merge`, `*-parallel`, `sorted_index_scan`,\n…)\n  pass unchanged.\n\n> Note: this closes the query-side path. The deterministic concurrency\n> reproduction (`toast-mutable-race-local.toml` from the issue) is the\nright tool\n> to exercise the race directly; the regress test here is a\nsingle-backend\n> visibility guard.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: Mithun Chicklore Yogendra <mithun.cy@gmail.com>",
