          "distinct": true,
          "id": "389c7f959945fb7b23228154a1536da5a9a51b4e",
          "message": "ci: register the `dst` crate with CODEOWNERS, dependabot and CI (#5640)\n\nFollow-up to #5639. That PR added `dst/` but the crate is invisible to\nthe repo's bookkeeping: nobody owns it, and nothing runs its tests or\nlints both of its feature configurations.\n\nAlso drops `(Antithesis)` from the crate description. Antithesis is one\nrunner of these properties, not what the crate is — `dst` wraps the SDK,\nbut the hooks are the abstraction.\n\n### Wiring the crate up\n\n- **`.github/workflows/test-dst-crate.yml`** — new. Clippy, rustdoc and\nthe unit tests, in both feature configurations, gated on `dst/**`. The\ncrate has no Postgres dependency, so it needs none of the pgrx setup the\npg_search workflows carry: plain `ubuntu-latest`, about a minute, and\nother Rust PRs don't pay for it.\n- **CODEOWNERS** — `/dst/` to `@paradedb/pg_search-maintainers`, like\nevery other crate.\n- **dependabot** — a `/dst` cargo entry, commented out to match the\nexisting `pg_search` and `tokenizers` ones.\n- **Cargo.toml** — workspace members sorted alphabetically.\n- **nix** — `cargoHash` refresh, pushed by the bot. #5639 changed\n`Cargo.lock`, so this fix was owed to that PR; `main` currently carries\na stale hash and this branch carries the correction.\n\nWhy both feature configurations, and why not just lean on lint-rust:\nstressgres pins `dst = { features = [\"enabled\"] }`, so feature\nunification turns `enabled` on for the whole workspace and `cargo clippy\n--workspace` only ever lints the SDK-linked half. The feature-off half —\nthe one pg_search actually ships — was never linted anywhere.\n\nThat unification is lint-only. Every packaging path is package-scoped\n(`cargo pgrx package --package pg_search`), so a released pg_search\nresolves `dst` with the feature off and does not link the SDK unless\nbuilt with `--features dst`.\n\n`dst` is deliberately absent from test-pg_search: it is a no-op in every\nnon-Antithesis build, so there is nothing there for the pg matrix to\ntest.\n\n### Path filter ordering\n\nUnrelated tidy-up, kept to its own commit and easy to drop. The `paths:`\nlists had accumulated in whatever order entries were added, differently\nin every workflow. One rule now: `.github/` first (a dot directory sorts\nto the top in the repo UI), then other directories alphabetically, then\nrepo-root files, then the `**/*.ext` catch-alls. Negations stay directly\nbeneath the pattern they subtract from, since GitHub applies path\nfilters in order. Only line positions move; the set of matched paths is\nunchanged.\n\nVerified locally: clippy, rustdoc and `cargo test -p dst` are clean in\nboth configurations, `cargo machete` is clean, and `cargo metadata\n--locked` plus taplo/prettier pass.\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01Grfu2vmdg2C3VqXxxqqzdr\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Philippe Noël <21990816+philippemnoel@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: paradedb-github-app[bot] <282009505+paradedb-github-app[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>",
