          "id": "5e774ad6638ef33029820272ca0a2838d1a91be8",
          "message": "feat: `partition_by` syntax and execution (#5679)\n\n# Ticket(s) Closed\n\n- Closes #5661\n\n## What\n\nAdd `partition_by` syntax (without a consumer), and support for adding a\n`RangePartitioningSample` to `ExecutionPlan`s to request that they be\nstatically range partitioned.\n\n## Why\n\nTo enable the optimizer rule from #5662 and #5663 to enable range\npartitioning in appropriate plan locations using samples that it has\ncollected.\n\n## How\n\nIntroduce the `RangePartitioningSample` and `RangePartitioning` types.\nThe former is used to construct the latter given a target partition\ncount, which is used to allow plans to re-partition themselves in order\nto \"scale\" a node via our `datafusion-distributed` `TaskEstimator`.\n\n## Tests\n\nNew unit tests, but the capability is not yet used in production code.",
          "timestamp": "2026-07-26T16:27:15-07:00",
          "tree_id": "0b8d69d1682f4b8e248acfddaaa10f023bab5a11",
