          "id": "f76ae3d221aa2445dd155cbdeeb31e15a02db9f8",
          "message": "feat: cap vector index build parallelism at 4 workers (#5837)\n\nIn experiments (and verified in CI), we don't see any appreciable\nbenefit in index build time beyond 4 parallel workers. The intuition is\nthat parallelizing the heap scan/segment flushes isn't the bottleneck,\nit's vector clustering/training which SuperKMeans already spreads out\nover all available cores (regardless of Postgres worker settings).\n\nHowever, using fewer workers saves memory because it means fewer\nconcurrent merges -> fewer concurrent clustering/assignment operations.",
