          "id": "8649e43d5fdfc3fdde29e41c42cb90f5cb4d0821",
          "message": "perf: Lazy vischeck for cardinality aggs over string fields (#5945)\n\n# Ticket(s) Closed\n\n- Closes #\n\n## What\n\nIn local testing, speeds up cardinality aggregates over a string field\nby ~47% when MVCC is enabled.\n\nThe idea is that we don't need to vischeck every value for a cardinality\nquery, we only need to do it when its value is not yet confirmed\nvisible. Additionally, this only works with string fields because\nTantivy uses a hyperloglog sketch for non string fields per segment,\nwhich erases information about what values have been seen. String fields\nget collected in a per-segment set of term ordinals, which allows\nmembership checking.\n\nDepends on https://github.com/paradedb/tantivy/pull/202\n\n## Why\n\n## How\n\n## Tests\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: paradedb-github-app[bot] <282009505+paradedb-github-app[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>",
