          "id": "c4c3574bfe48eff253169009c694c35463e70a68",
          "message": "perf: Enable block-WAND optimization on score-ordered joins (#5487)\n\n# Ticket(s) Closed\n- Closes #5300 \n\n## What\nEnable the use of block-max-wand in score-ordered top-k queries\nrestricted by a join.\n\n## Why\nSpeeeeeed 🐎 \n\n## How\n- Update to a version of tantivy that gives us access to\n`Weight::pruning_scorer()`, allowing tantivy to use a\nblock-wand-oriented `PruningScorer` if the query supports it, and a\nbasic pruning scorer otherwise.\n- Modify `DeferredScorer` to use `pruning_scorer`, and thread the wiring\nfor setting the threshold up to the batch scanner.\n- Add a mechanism for extracting a score threshold from DataFusion's\ndynamic filters as part of each loop.\n\n## Tests\n- New unit tests for threshold extraction\n- All existing tests pass\n- Local verification that the performance of\n`join_top_k-score-desc-high-selectivity.sql` query gets ~2x faster with\nthis in place (~250ms to ~120ms) on the 1m row stack overflow dataset.\n- `join_top_k-score-desc-high-selectivity` benchmark shows pruning was\napplied: ~3x speedup on the 20m dataset.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: paradedb-github-app[bot] <282009505+paradedb-github-app[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>",
          "timestamp": "2026-07-10T10:47:40-06:00",
