          "distinct": true,
          "id": "0335f5708b87a531cddb1438d554eb2362274f7f",
          "message": "fix(benchmarks): bind the query vector for reference plans too (#5829)\n\nRegression from #5789, which failed both regenerated baseline runs at\nthe 1m stage:\n\n```\nError: `knn_top10_10pct - alternative 1` reads cohere.qvec but no query vectors were loaded;\nthe dataset's recall fixtures must be present for a vector benchmark\n```\n\n#5789 stopped reference plans from taking one sample per held-out vector\nby handing them an empty vector slice. But an empty slice already meant\nsomething else — \"no recall fixtures loaded\" — which is a hard error for\nany query that reads the vector GUC. A reference plan reads it exactly\nlike a swept one; it just should not iterate all 100.\n\nPass the vectors either way, and let a separate `sample_per_vector` flag\ndecide whether to iterate them. The saving #5789 intended is unchanged:\nalternatives still take `--runs` samples rather than 200.\n\nThe precondition is now a named `reads_query_vector` with a test pinning\nthat it tracks vector *availability* and never sampling mode — that\nconflation is what broke.",
          "timestamp": "2026-08-03T12:20:03-07:00",
          "tree_id": "8d5f97b84de2b0fa91e89d3203db0c94d6f9f83a",
