          "id": "2d3668858dcb8ad4e1392dec22a99358bc76506d",
          "message": "fix: Bound seqscan memory by spilling to `BufFile` (#5539)\n\n# Ticket(s) Closed\n\n- Closes #\n\n## What\n\nThe sequential scan materialized the entire result set, which means\nunbounded memory over large result sets. Instead, we now bound the size\nof the in memory set, then spill it to an externally-sorted `BufFile`\nfronted by an in memory sparse index for fast searching.\n\nAdditionally:\n\n- Added a cheap always true/false path for pure `all`/`exists` queries\n- The sequential scan also emits a once-per-statement WARNING when the\nBM25 index isn't being used, and when we spill to a temp file\n\n## Why\n\n## How\n\nI also considered implementing something that evaluates the query\nagainst every row inline, but that would mean re-implementing\ntokenization + Tantivy query types to get parity with our current\nseqscan support. In the end it was too complex and I felt this approach\nwas much simpler.\n\n## Tests",
