          "id": "3aa2795d3a3d273f887d3ba0faec2d596b8520a3",
          "message": "perf: remove pgrx overhead during visibility checking (#5306)\n\nThe pgrx library wraps all of the C bindings in pg_guard which ensures\nthat Rust properly unwinds the stack when a Postgres function encounters\nan error. This is required for safety reasons but adds substantial\noverhead to certain functions that are very short. In this case checking\nthe visibility map to determine if a block is all visible is simply a\ncouple bit manipulations which the pg_guard wrapper adds substantial\noverhead too.\n\nThis change adds a raw binding to the visibilitymap_get_status function\nbypassing the pgrx implementation only when we know its safe to do so.\nThis results in ~10% performance improvement for queries that heavily\nuse the visibility map for visibility checking.\n\n# Ticket(s) Closed\n\n- Closes #5265 \n\n## What\n\n## Why\n\n## How\n\n## Tests",
          "timestamp": "2026-06-18T09:26:05-07:00",
