          "id": "f91e37b12aa3839344892da52bd4b999d6bc4cca",
          "message": "fix: EXPLAIN on aggregate join with heap filter no longer panics (#5542)\n\n# Ticket(s) Closed\n\n- Closes #5514\n\n---\nWhat\n\nEXPLAIN (and EXPLAIN ANALYZE) on an aggregate join query with a\nheap-filter predicate (e.g. ILIKE) no longer crashes with ERROR: XX000:\nAn expression context must be provided when heap filtering.\n\nWhy\n\nDuring EXPLAIN-only mode, begin_custom_scan skips allocating an\nExprContext since no expressions actually run. But explain_custom_scan\nwas still calling render_df_physical_plan, which tried to build a full\nDataFusion physical plan. Building that plan triggers\nPgSearchTableProvider::scan() → SearchIndexReader::open_with_context() →\ninto_tantivy_query(), and heap-filter predicates require a live\nExprContext at that point so it panicked.\n\nHow\n\n- In render_df_physical_plan, check upfront whether any source query\ncontains a HeapFilter. If so, skip physical plan rendering and emit an\ninformative note instead.\n- Convert the .expect() in into_tantivy_query_generic and\n.unwrap_or_else(panic) in open_with_context to proper Err propagation as\na defensive backstop for any future caller that bypasses the guard.\n\nTests\n\nAdded test_explain_aggregate_join_with_heap_filter covering the exact\nrepro from the issue both EXPLAIN and EXPLAIN ANALYZE with @@@ + ILIKE\non a joined aggregate query with both enable_aggregate_custom_scan and\nenable_join_custom_scan on.\n\ncc : @rebasedming\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Stu Hood <stuhood@gmail.com>",
