          "id": "3b073d94ea600cc327e70ca2ef0f426a99189658",
          "message": "test: Ride out post-fault recovery in the Antithesis index-consistency check (#5948)\n\nFollow-up to #5915, which merged before this fix landed on the branch.\n\nThe 30x2s retry loop in `eventually_verify_index_consistency.sh` fails\nwhen the database is still mid-recovery: faults stop when an eventually\ncommand starts, but the cluster takes time to become operational again.\nA 60-minute Antithesis validation run showed 305 timelines failing on\nconnection errors alone, with no index ever inconsistent.\n\nReplace the fixed attempt count with a longer deadline loop and report\nthe last real error on failure, so an unreachable database and an\ninconsistent index are distinguishable in the report. A follow-up\n60-minute run with this version passed the check on all 332 timelines.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>",
