          "id": "4581c7960edc4ca0147a83e8f5e01072ca992bb2",
          "message": "refactor(mpp): remove columnar sort and its dependent code (#5439)\n\n## What\n\nThis PR removes the `enable_columnar_sort` GUC and all the code that\ndepended on it.\n\n## Why\n\n`enable_columnar_sort` was the only thing that lowered a scan to the\nmulti-partition/sorted shape the MPP dispatch codec can't ship. With it\ngone, every scan is a single-partition lazy leaf, so no plan is ever\nundispatchable, which is the end state MPP-by-default needs.\n\nRather than detect the undispatchable shape at launch and fall back to\nserial, we remove the feature that produced it. The `sort_by` index\noption and the `ColumnarExecState` path itself stay; only the query-time\ncolumnar sort / SortMergeJoin lowering is removed.\n\n## Removed\n\n- `SortMergeJoinEnforcer` (`joinscan/planner.rs`), and the `orderby.rs`\n`sort_by_pathkey` chain.\n- `sort_order` plumbing through `JoinSource`/`ScanInfo`, and\n`table_provider`'s eager/throttled scans.\n- `ColumnarExecStrategy::Sorted`, `create_sorted_scan`, the\n`SortPreservingMergeExec` wrapping, and the\n`ScanRecipe::Eager`/`Prefetched` variants.\n\n## Tests\n\nRegress is green. The sorted-scan and SMJ tests were renamed to\n`index_order_by` / `join_order_by`, with their expectations updated to\nthe non-columnar-sort plans (results unchanged).",
          "timestamp": "2026-07-07T01:14:58-07:00",
          "tree_id": "340242031514e67366e56dee5533341f8d3f8082",
          "url": "https://github.com/paradedb/paradedb/commit/4581c7960edc4ca0147a83e8f5e01072ca992bb2"
