          "distinct": true,
          "id": "13c347842b75e18fc63c887ae0c489383565deeb",
          "message": "fix: quoted mixed-case table aliases in custom scans (#5551)\n\n# Ticket(s) Closed\n\n- Closes #5525\n\n## What\n\nFixes `FieldNotFound` errors when the aggregate custom scan or the join\ncustom scan run against a query with a quoted mixed-case table alias\n(e.g. `parent AS \"Parent\"`, as Sequelize emits by default). Both trigger\nsites from #5525 are covered by a single fix at the centralized alias\nemitter.\n\n## Why\n\n`RelationAlias::execution` preserved the original alias case (`\"Parent\"\n→ \"Parent_0\"`). Downstream:\n\n- Schema registration (`ctx.register_table`, `df.alias`) parses the\nidentifier through DataFusion's `parse_str`, which case-folds unquoted\nidentifiers, so the schema qualifies `parent_0`.\n- Column references built via `make_col` use `TableReference::Bare` to\nskip parsing (per its own doc comment), so they preserve case and\nreference `\"Parent_0\"`.\n\nThe two sides no longer agree → `FieldNotFound`.\n\n## How\n\nLowercase the alias inside `RelationAlias::execution` — the single point\nfrom which all eight DataFusion-facing alias sites originate (verified\nvia grep across\n`pg_search/src/postgres/customscan/{joinscan,aggregatescan,datafusion}/`).\n`parse_str` and `TableReference::Bare` now receive the same\nalready-lowercased string, so schema qualification and column references\nagree.\n\n`RelationAlias::display` (used for EXPLAIN output) and\n`RelationAlias::warning_context` (used for planner warnings) are\nseparate methods and continue to preserve case — EXPLAIN output is\nunaffected.\n\n## Tests\n\nNew `pg_regress` test `alias_quoted_mixed_case.sql` covering both\ntrigger sites from #5525:\n\n- **Trigger 1**: `count(\"Parent\".\"id\")` over a join with quoted\nmixed-case aliases (aggregate custom scan). Previously crashed with `No\nfield named \"Parent_0\".id`; now `EXPLAIN` shows `Custom Scan (ParadeDB\nAggregate Scan)` engaging cleanly.\n- **Trigger 2**: `@@@` predicate + `ORDER BY` fast field with quoted\nmixed-case aliases (join custom scan). Previously crashed with\n`FieldNotFound \"Child_0\".ctid_0`; now `EXPLAIN` shows `Custom Scan\n(ParadeDB Join Scan)` engaging cleanly.\n- **Parity**: identical queries with the relevant custom scan disabled\nfall back to native Postgres and return identical results.\n- **Controls**: identical queries with lowercase (unquoted) aliases —\nwhich always worked — continue to return identical results.\n\nLocally verified with a revert-then-run cycle: reverting only the\none-line fix reproduces the exact issue error message (`Failed to build\nDataFusion aggregate plan: Schema error: No field named \"Parent_0\".id\n...`), confirming the test genuinely exercises the bug. Full pg_regress\nsuite (297 tests) passes with the change applied.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Mithun Chicklore Yogendra <mithun.cy@gmail.com>",
