          "message": "chore: Upgrade to datafusion 55 (#5634)\n\n# Ticket(s) Closed\n - Closes #5553 \n\n## What\nUpdates to pre-release DataFusion 55 and a DataFusion Distributed rev\nbased on DF 55.\n\n## Why\nDataFusion 55 has range partitioning functionality we need for future\nwork.\n\n## How\nMostly update `cargo.toml` and fix compile errors. \n\nThere is one additional wrinkle: In DF 55, `HashJoinExec` changes its\nbehavior to fix a bug (See\n[this](https://github.com/apache/datafusion/pull/22523)). That change\nassumes that installed dynamic filters remain installed between filter\npushdown passes. This PR includes a change to make our handling of\nfilter pushdown compatible by retaining filters between passes and\nde-duping by expression id. There is a lingering issue (#5635) from\nthat, to be addressed later.\n\n## Tests\n- All unit and integration tests pass\n- Regression test output updates fall into 4 categories:\n- Join order or type changes do to planning changes between DF 54 & 55.\n  - Cosmetic changes in the printed node info for `HashJoinExec`\n- +1 increases in dynamic filter counts. This is fine. It's due to the\nissue mentioned above and will be fixed separately. The orphaned filter\nis just `lit(true)`, so there are no correctness issues.\n  - The addition of a `null_aware` to some lines.:\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: paradedb-github-app[bot] <282009505+paradedb-github-app[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Mohammad Dashti <mdashti@gmail.com>",
