          "distinct": true,
          "id": "a974d2eecc3fd3b5027236b70ab951577c15615c",
          "message": "ci: tune cohere hnsw ef_search for ~95% recall@10 (#5490)\n\n## What\n\nReplaces the untuned `ef_search` placeholders in the cohere benchmark\nwith size-scaled values, so the HNSW recall CI reports at a real ~95%\nrecall@10 operating point (matching how ivfflat `probes` are already\ntuned per `dataset_size`).\n\n## Values\n\nMeasured locally by building HNSW (`vector_cosine_ops`, default m=16 /\nef_construction=64) and sweeping `ef_search` against the exact S3 ground\ntruth over 100 held-out queries:\n\n| query | 1M ef_search | recall@10 | notes |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `knn_top10_unfiltered` | **115** | 0.954 | was hardcoded `100`\n(0.946); now a `{{ ef_search_unfiltered }}` param like the others |\n| `knn_top10_10pct` | **280** | 0.951 | |\n| `knn_top10_1pct` | **400** + scan caps | ~0.93 | see below |\n\n### `knn_top10_1pct` cannot reach 95% via `ef_search`\n\nFor a ~1% filter, HNSW does post-filtering with iterative scan. Recall\nis bounded by the iterative-scan budget (`hnsw.max_scan_tuples`),\n**not** beam width — so raising `ef_search` is nearly flat (0.77→0.80\nacross ef 40→400). The best we found was ~0.93 with a 10× scan budget\n(`max_scan_tuples=200000`, `scan_mem_multiplier=4`, `ef_search=400`), so\nthe 1% query now sets those too. Per the instruction, since 95% is\nunreachable this uses the best params found. The exact pre-filter\n(variant 2) remains the accurate path for a filter this selective.\n\n## 10M values are extrapolated\n\nThe 10M HNSW build is a multi-hour job that couldn't be completed on the\ntest box, so the 10M `ef_search` values are **estimated** from the 1M\ncrossover, scaled by this dataset's own ivfflat probe growth (~1.6–2×\nfor 10× rows) and rounded up for safety. `ef_search` is size-scaled (via\n`CASE dataset_size`) because HNSW recall at a fixed `ef_search` declines\nas the corpus grows. **These 10M values should be confirmed by an actual\n10M sweep** and adjusted if they over/under-shoot.\n\n## Files\n- `config.toml` — `ef_search_*` now size-scaled `CASE` expressions;\nadded `ef_search_unfiltered`, `max_scan_tuples_1pct`,\n`scan_mem_multiplier_1pct`.\n- `queries/knn_top10_unfiltered.sql` — hardcoded `ef_search=100` → `{{\nef_search_unfiltered }}`.\n- `queries/knn_top10_1pct.sql` — variant 1 now sets the iterative-scan\ncaps.",
