          "id": "55d07ba83d45b17711a6124a0ce48af3e3710d8f",
          "message": "ci(antithesis): build schema in a fault-free first_ command (#5563)\n\nFollow-up to #5521.\n\n## What\n\nBuild each suite's schema in a fault-free `first_` command instead of\ninside the driver, and drop the startup timeout #5521 added as a\nstopgap.\n\n- New `SetupMode`: `--setup-only` (build schema, exit) for `first_`;\n`--skip-setup` (workload only, no teardown) for the driver; default is\nthe full lifecycle.\n- One test template per suite: `first_<suite>` (rewrite connstr,\n`--setup-only`) + `singleton_driver_<suite>` (`--skip-setup`) + a copy\nof the shared `anytime_recovery_liveness`.\n- Also: reconnect-grace baseline 1h → 200s, and metric lines now write\nin one call so a killed process can't emit a torn JSON line.\n\n## Why\n\nSetup ran on the fault path, where a fault straddling the schema build\ncould pin the driver for the whole grace (what the startup timeout\nworked around). A `first_` command runs before any fault injection, so\nbuilding the schema there removes the straddle and the bound. Per-suite\ntemplates keep suites from colliding on the shared `paradedb-rw` schema\n(two templates never share a timeline) and bound a timeline's disk to\none suite.\n\n## Tests\n\n`cargo test -p stressgres` / `clippy` / `shellcheck` green. Drove all\nthree modes against local Postgres (setup-only builds then exits,\nskip-setup runs the workload without touching the schema, full run tears\ndown). The Antithesis run surfaced a pre-existing pg_search bug (#5566),\nnot a PR defect.\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Philippe Noël <21990816+philippemnoel@users.noreply.github.com>",
